<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Helena Kantakouzene</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. after 1394</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Helena Kantakouzene was a Byzantine noblewoman, granddaughter of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-vi-kantakouzenos">John VI Kantakouzenos</a>, who married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-fadrique">Louis Fadrique</a>, Count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amfissa">Salona</a>. After his death in 1382 she governed the county for their daughter Maria. In 1394 she surrendered Salona to the Ottoman sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayezid-i">Bayezid I</a>, and her daughter was taken into his harem.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1394 the widow of Louis Fadrique, <b>Helena Kantakouzene</b>, lost Salona to Sultan Bayezid I. It was briefly held by the Despotate of the Morea and the Knights Hospitaller in the early 15th century before the Ottomans took it permanently in 1410.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-salona">County of Salona</a></li></ul></section>
